+## AGC 26.2 alpha18 - integrated semantic tick plan
+
+Alpha18 moves from separate optimisation kernels to a single integrated semantic tick plan. The new plan is still no-invasion: Bukkit-visible mutation, plugin events, entity ticks, redstone, block/entity ticks, chunk FIFO and per-connection packet order remain ordered. The new work is algorithmic:
+
+- `AGCUnifiedTickPlanCompiler` builds one tick-local plan for network, chunk, entity, world and plugin helper work.
+- `AGCNetworkSendGraphCompiler` compiles lossless recipient send graphs without packet drops, mutable packet sharing or connection reordering.
+- `AGCChunkSpatialRoutePlanner` creates stable chunk route keys and route hints without changing Paper chunk queue ordering.
+- `AGCEntityTrackerDeltaIndex` prepares read-only tracker delta bands without skipping AI/tick/damage/interaction.
+- `AGCReadOnlyWorkStealingPlanner` reserves CPU for primary-thread, Netty, GC and plugins, then plans only read-only helper work on spare capacity.
+- `AGCPluginSemanticFirewall` classifies plugin work conservatively and sends Bukkit-visible operations to ordered primary-thread commit.
+- `/agc scale18` reports the integrated plan.
+
+This is meant to push the thousand-player survival target by improving algorithms, not by degrading gameplay semantics.
